---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
		<style>
			.container {
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				justify-content: flex-start;
			}

			.child-item {
				align-self: center;
			}

			img {
				max-height: 512px;
				max-width: 256px;
			}

			.profile-pic {
				max-width: 100px;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h2>Repair Prices</h2>
			<p class="child-item">
				I'm revising how I handle my pricing since things were overly complicated before. 
				<br/>
				<br/>
				Diagnosing the issue with your instrument or gear will always be free. 
				<br/>
				<br/>
				I charge <strong>$100 per hour</strong> for repairs based on 15 minute intervals 
				(so if it only takes me 15 minutes I'll only charge $25, $50 for a half hour and so-on) for labor. 
				This is basically the same amount I was charging before, just not pages and pages broken down 
				per instrument/equipment.  
				<br/>
				<br/>
				No repair is too big or small and I won't charge you $80 for a 10 second repair
				where all I did was adjust a screw. (I wouldn't even charge for that to be honest).
				part of being a local shop is, I won't charge if there isn't actually anything significant
				wrong.
				<br />
				<br />
				Parts costs will also be the responsibility of the customer. 
				I don't usually mark up parts, other than for sales tax if I got 
				the part wholesale, or to round up or down to the nearest dollar for ease of transactions.
				<br/>
				<br/>
				All repairs come with a satisfaction guarantee, I know often instruments
				for schools often sit around unplayed for a while after a repair,
				so if I missed something related to the same issue, I'll look at it
				no cost to you.
				<br />
				<br />
				I also price match other local repair shops, if any repair I quote
				would be cheaper at somewhere in the greater Seattle area that's drivable
				(within reason, we're not talking road trip here) from my shop, I'll
				match their price and even change the price here to match.
			</p>
			<h2>What I Repair</h2>
			<p class="child-item">
				Because I shrank this page down I'll make a list of the instruments and gear I service:
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Brass Instruments:</strong> Tuba, Trombone, Trumpet, French Horn, and all related brass instruments!
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Woodwind Instruments:</strong> Flute, Clarinet, Saxophones, Oboe, Bassoon, and all related instruments!
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Electric Instruments:</strong> Electric Guitar, Electric Bass, Electric Keyboards, Electric Violin and similar.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Stringed Acoustic Instruments:</strong> Acoustic Guitar, Banjo, other similar instruments. (I do not yet work on violin/viola/cello/bass but I am learning)
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Percussion:</strong> Drums, cymbals, other similar percussion instruments.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Music related electronic gear:</strong> Amplifiers, Microphones, Patch cables, PA Systems, some other types of electronic gear, just ask!
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Other:</strong> Accordion repair.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
						<h2>COMING SOON</h2>
			<p class="child-item">
				Stuff I am learning to repair/do or that I want to service and support.  If these services interest you
				please reach out. Knowing that people need the service will motivate me to focus on adding that to my repertoire faster:
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Orchestral Strings/Luthier:</strong> violin/viola/cello/bass
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Piano Repair and Tuning</strong>
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Music Production and Sound Engineering</strong>: Including live performance setup and support, and music production services.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Lessons:</strong> I don't currently give lessons, but in the future if time permits I might consider it.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Supplies Sales:</strong> Reeds, Cork grease, slide oil, cleaning supplies, guitar strings...etc.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Other?:</strong> If it's music related and Duvall or the Eastside is lacking it, I am willing to learn. message me!
					</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
			<Footer />
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
